ile†L32】\n\n**Final field values**\n\n| Field          | Value |\n|----------------|-------|\n| `record.partialClose` | `true` |\n| `record.status`       | `'partial'` |\n| `record.finalClose`   | `true` |\n\n**Consistency check** – The artifact’s *proof contract* states that a *partial* close should **not** be simultaneously marked as a *final* close. Here both `partialClose` **and** `finalClose` are `true`, which is **internally inconsistent** and therefore **breaks the contract**.\n\n**`|| 0` defaults used in the function**\n\n- `fill.closedQuantity || 0` (line 22) – provides a default of `0` when `closedQuantity` is falsy.  \n- `record.entryQuantity || 0` (line 23) – provides a default of `0` when `entryQuantity` is falsy.  \n\n*Both defaults are present in the source*【open_file†L22-L23】.\n\n---\n\n### RECONCILIATION OF PRIOR AST‑SCAN CLAIM\n\nThe earlier answer claimed “per‑file AST scans across 8 files”. Telemetry shows only **one** `serena_method_callers` invocation, which scanned **only the canary file**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"method\":\"publishCloseProof\",\n  \"total\":0,\n  \"filesScanned\":1,\n  \"callers\":[]\n}\n```\n\n*Citation*: `serena_method_callers` result【serena_method_callers†L1-L8】.\n\nThus the prior claim was inaccurate; the single scan covered the canary artifact and found **zero callers**.\n\n---\n\n## VERDICT UPDATE\n\nThe original verdict that “the canary artifact remains safely isolated and its proof contract cannot be broken” is **incorrect**.  \nThe artifact itself violates its contract by unconditionally setting `record.finalClose = true` while also setting `record.partialClose = true` and `record.status = 'partial'`. This constitutes a **substantive break** of the intended “close proof” semantics.\n\n**Revised verdict:** **CONTRACT BREAK DETECTED** – the canary artifact fails its own proof contract. The earlier conclusion must be overturned.","tool_calls":null,"tool_call_id":null},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":15881,"